[33.84, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I've written the plan for the cycling app and saved it to `/cfg/plans/make-a-plan-for-vectorized-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  origami.md`. Nothing has been built yet.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Stack:** Expo with TypeScript and Expo Router, Mapbox for maps, and Supabase (Postgres with PostGIS) as\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the backend. Background GPS needs EAS dev builds, not Expo Go.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **MVP:** Ride recording that works offline, a social feed (follows, kudos, comments), XP, levels, streaks,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  badges, weekly challenges, segments with leaderboards, clubs, and push notifications.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **v2:** Territory capture on the map, group rides, sensor and health integrations, and safety features.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Timeline:** About 16 weeks. Ride recording comes first because background GPS and battery use are the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  biggest technical risk.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cheating and privacy:** Gamification rules and anti-cheat checks run on the server. Privacy zones hide\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  start and end points.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Verification:** Unit tests for the XP, streak and badge rules, database tests for segment matching and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  access rules, and field rides checked against a bike computer. There is also an end-to-end flow test and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  TestFlight/Play internal beta.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The plan lists four open questions, and I assumed Supabase for the fourth:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Which platforms to launch on (iOS first, or both).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Whether to focus on road, mountain biking or both.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - How to make money.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Whether you prefer a different backend.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[44.724, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Here are my answers to the four open questions:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  - **Platforms:** Launch on iOS and Android together. Cyclists are split pretty evenly across both, and Expo\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  makes it cheap to do both.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  - **Focus:** Road cycling first, including gravel. The segments, leaderboards and streaks fit road riders\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  best, and mountain biking can come later.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  - **Money:** Free to use, with an optional paid tier for things like advanced stats, extra challenges and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  club tools. Core ride recording and the social features stay free so the community can grow.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  - **Backend:** Supabase is fine, so keep it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  Please update the plan with these answers and finish it.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
